# Language-model API keys for the container deployment -- a TEMPLATE, holding no key.
#
# Copy it to `deployment/docker/llm-keys.env` (git-ignored, never copied into the image), put the
# keys you use there, and restart the workspace:
#
#     docker compose up -d --force-recreate web
#
# Then, in LLM settings, add the connection with "an environment variable of this workspace" and the
# variable's NAME (e.g. OPENAI_API_KEY). The workspace stores that reference and a fingerprint; the
# key itself is never stored, shown or logged. A LOCAL model (the host's Ollama) needs no key.

# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
